# HTML Standards

## Structure

- Single-page app: `index.html` is the entry point. Keep semantic structure (`button`, `label`, `ul`, `form`).
- `lang="en"` on `<html>` is set; UI text is French — do not change language attributes without approval.

## Class Naming

- **BEM with underscores**: `block__element`, `block__element--modifier` (e.g. `panel_box__title`, `track_display__half--cover`).
- **`js-` prefix** for JavaScript hooks only (`js-login-button`, `js-answers`). Never use `js-` classes for styling.
- **State classes** toggled by JS: `visible`, `active`, `hidden`, `game_started`, `game_ended`, `playing`, `correct`, `incorrect`.

## Accessibility

- Interactive icons must have `aria-label` and `title` (see `bar_top__logout`).
- Associate labels with inputs via `for` / `id`.
- Decorative images: `role="decoration"` where appropriate.

## Glitch Text Pattern

Dual spans for glitch effect — keep both versions in sync:

```html
<span class="text_no_glitch">Paramètres</span>
<span class="text_glitch">…glitched unicode…</span>
```

## Scripts

Load order: jQuery → `js/app.js` (`type="module"`). Do not reorder without verifying dependencies.
